   "body": "## Meanwhile, the future is already hiring\n\nAI. Climate. Biotech. Robotics. Space.\n\nSome of these jobs are too new for your parents to have looked up yet, and some only got a name recently. The talk gives one instruction for this section: skip the sci-fi costume. Every field below comes with a sentence about the work people are actually doing.\n\nThe goal isn't to make you panic about being late to a job. It's to help you get curious early.\n\n## AI: AI Ethicist for Schools\n\n*Decides what a classroom should never hand over to an AI model.*\n\nThis one isn't about building the technology. It's about judgement: what a school should keep human, and why. Students who argue well and notice unfairness quickly might feel at home here.\n\nRelated from the game: the **Conversation Designer**, who writes how an AI talks to millions of people, and when it should stop.\n\n## Climate: Heat-action Planner\n\n*Keeps a city breathable in a May that keeps getting longer.*\n\nFrom the atlas tour, the same job designs cities that don't cook their poorest residents. It mixes care for people with planning.\n\nClimate also has the **Carbon Accountant**, who counts a company's invisible exhaust the way a CA counts money.\n\n## Biotech: Cultured Meat Designer\n\n*Grows a kebab without a farm. It's a long road, but it's already a job.*\n\nBiotech also has quieter roles, like the **Genetic Counsellor**, who sits with a family while a blood test turns into a life decision.\n\n## Robotics: Personal Robot Trainer\n\n*Teaches a home robot the difference between a guest and a burglar.*\n\nThe robot can't learn that on its own. Someone patient has to teach it what matters in a real home.\n\n## Space: Space Habitat Gardener\n\n*Grows salad in a tin can, far from any rain.*\n\nBack on Earth, the **Satellite Imagery Analyst** reads crops, floods and forests from orbit.\n\n## Climate, again: Coral Restoration Diver\n\n*Gardens the reef while the water still allows it.*\n\n## How to go deeper\n\nIf one field lights you up, go deep on it. If none do yet, treat this page as a tasting menu and come back later.\n\nDay 15 of **Thirty Days of Looking** gives you a simple exercise: read one article about AI, climate, biotech, robots or space, and circle the jobs hiding in the paragraph. There are usually more than you'd expect.",
