   "body": "## After a loud hour, a quiet line\n\nThe talk ends almost in a whisper:\n\n**Don't choose the most popular career.**\n\nThen a pause, and a smile:\n\n**Choose the career that fits you.**\n\nFit takes work. You get it from the six lenses, from honest Tuesdays, and from the slow chain of exposure, curiosity, practice and identity. **Exposure is what makes fit possible.** You can't find out what fits until you've seen more than six options.\n\n## The only homework\n\n> Stay curious. Keep exposing yourself.\n> A wider map is a kind of kindness to the adult you are becoming.\n\nIf you only remember three things from this series, make them these:\n\n1. **Open the atlas.** Read it slowly. Say the strange names out loud.\n2. **Start Day 1.** Five minutes. Every career you can name. Keep the list.\n3. **Play the game with a friend.** Ten clues. Count your wrong answers, because that's your gap.\n\nCAM is a movement, not a verdict. It won't tell you what to become. It'll keep showing you what's out there.\n\n## One last exercise\n\nThe talk ends by asking one student to name a job they heard about that day for the first time, and then it stops on that name.\n\nDo the same now. Write one job you didn't know existed before you started reading. That's where your map starts getting wider.\n\n**Exposure is all you need.**",
