   "body": "## Exposure is all you need\n\n**CAM, the Career Advisory Movement**, is a keynote and an atlas for Classes 8 to 12. CAM is an initiative of VOYCE.\n\nIt makes one promise and keeps it: **we don't pick a life for you. We show you that a six-item menu was never the whole world.**\n\n## Two co-founders, one wider map\n\n**Suryavamshi** and **Ariba** built CAM so that a class of fourteen-year-olds would meet more than six jobs before they ever saw a subject-choice form.\n\nThe idea behind it is simple. Students aren't short of ambition. They're short of exposure. You can only choose from what you've seen, and most students have been shown about twelve careers. CAM exists to widen that view early enough for it to matter.\n\n## The pieces\n\nCAM comes in four parts, and they all do the same job: offering a wider map in time.\n\n- **The talk.** *Exposure Is All You Need*, a keynote that moves from the uncle's question at a wedding to the Exposure Gap, the chain of interest, the six lenses and a quiet close. It's available here as a series of articles.\n- **The atlas.** 2,000+ careers across 88 industries, the ones school forgot to name.\n- **The game.** *Guess the job*: ten clues from real Tuesdays. Wrong answers show the Exposure Gap.\n- **Thirty days of looking.** One small task a day, so you don't have to decide your whole life this week.\n\n## For schools and teachers\n\nIf your school has a room that needs a wider view, CAM visits schools to run the talk. Write to us with questions or to ask about a visit.\n\n## Write to us, follow along\n\n- **Email:** voycexx@gmail.com\n- **Instagram:** @cam.voyce\n- **X:** @InfoDeckAI\n\n*CAM is an initiative of VOYCE.*",
